From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:22:59 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 193/207] dsv41 runner: answer-commit behind
 TF_DSV41_RUNNER_COMMIT (off by default)

When the engine owns the value of the task's own closed expression, the
reasoning closes right after that result (the server's think close) and
the answer is the value verbatim, then EOS. The forced tokens go through
the same stream commit as every owned result.

It fires only where the r7 oracle can check it: an owned fence, REPL or
inline cell whose span is the one literal expression the last user
message states (no other number in it; a sum or product may be written
the other way round), a one-line integer value, cell records on, inside
the think block, outside a fence, trace line, EOS hand-off or tool call,
no tools offered, no compute-lane hold, and room for every forced token
within max_tokens and the answer quota. It fires once; after it the
scanner sees nothing and the EOS is no hand-off. Each firing is a
top-level "commit" receipt record (cell, span, value, field, at, token,
close_token, ids, landed).

Not built: the "final owned cell of a run" trigger without whole-task
coverage (the oracle cannot check that it answers the task); program
tasks (MBPP, algo) and true division never fire.

Knob off: replies and receipts byte-identical (tests); every guard has a
mutation case and a source negative control.
